user_prompt_template:
TUTORIAL REQUEST: {life_event}
SKILL LEVEL / AUDIENCE: {audience}
OUTPUT STYLE: {tone}
TUTORIAL TYPE: {formatting_profile}
DEPTH: {artifact_density}
ADDITIONAL CONTEXT: {context}

Design a complete tutorial framing for this request. Every field is mandatory. Be specific to this exact tutorial — no generic frameworks, no placeholder values, no output that could apply to a different topic.

Before writing, ask yourself: could any of these fields apply to a completely different tutorial? If yes, rewrite until they cannot.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "system_name": "A specific tutorial title that reads as custom-designed for this exact request. Must reflect the project/topic immediately.",
  "life_event": "The tutorial request exactly as provided",
  "operating_premise": "One sentence naming the specific learning challenge — skill gap, complexity, or risk the learner faces without this walkthrough.",
  "system_objective": "One sentence: the single measurable outcome — what the learner will have built, deployed, or demonstrated when done.",
  "time_horizon": "Realistic tutorial duration — e.g. '2–4 hours for beginners', '45-minute quick start', 'multi-session deep dive over 1–2 days'",
  "control_domains": [
    {{
      "id": "module-01",
      "name": "Specific module name that could not apply to any other tutorial",
      "purpose": "What specific skill or implementation milestone this module delivers",
      "scope_in": ["Specific activities, files, or concepts covered here"],
      "scope_out": ["Specific topics explicitly deferred to later modules or prerequisites"],
      "primary_outputs": ["Tangible deliverables: working feature, passing test, deployed URL, config file"]
    }}
  ],
  "key_roles": [
    {{
      "role": "Specific role for this tutorial context",
      "responsibility": "What this role does during the walkthrough",
      "authority_level": "learner | reviewer | deployer | observer"
    }}
  ],
  "critical_milestones": [
    {{
      "milestone": "Specific checkpoint name",
      "description": "How to verify this milestone — command output, URL, UI state, or test result",
      "sequence": 1
    }}
  ],
  "success_criteria": ["Verifiable outcome with a concrete threshold — not 'completion'"],
  "failure_modes": ["Specific mistake learners make in this tutorial and its consequence"],
  "operating_constraints": ["Stack, platform, time budget, or tool constraints from the request"]
}}
